"""gap-fill-2000-04, General Information: R.A. 6713 items on provisions the bank does not test yet.
Every item carries the exact LawPhil sentence it rests on (source_quote); the build checks each quote against the LawPhil text.
Facts already in the bank (8 norms, Sec. 5(a)-(e), Sec. 7(a)-(d) basics and souvenir rule, SALN deadlines and 10-working-day copying,
Sec. 9 30/60 days, Sec. 6 co-chairs, Sec. 11 six months' salary and 5 years, Sec. 3(b), 3(i), 3(j), Sec. 10(a), Sec. 12 CSC) are avoided."""
S, W, N, R = "GI-SIBLING-TERM", "GI-WRONG-BODY", "GI-NEIGHBOR-NUMBER", "GI-SOUNDS-RIGHT"
# (fact_id, archetype, section, difficulty, stem, key, [(distractor, code, why)], terms, shortcut, quote)
ITEMS = [
("RA6713-3A-GOVERNMENT-GOCC", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 3(a)", "easy",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 3(a), which of these is expressly included in the term \"Government\"?",
 "Government-owned or controlled corporations and their subsidiaries",
 [("Private schools that receive government scholarship funds", R, "Receiving public funds does not make a private school part of \"Government\" under Sec. 3(a)."),
  ("Political parties accredited by the Commission on Elections", R, "Accreditation by COMELEC does not make a party a government instrumentality; Sec. 3(a) does not list parties."),
  ("Private contractors while they carry out government infrastructure projects", R, "A contractor stays a private party; Sec. 3(a) covers agencies, local governments, GOCCs and their subsidiaries.")],
 "\"Government\" (Sec. 3(a)): the National Government, local governments, and all instrumentalities, agencies or branches, including GOCCs and their subsidiaries.",
 "If the State owns or controls it, including a GOCC's subsidiary, it is \"Government\".",
 "including government-owned or controlled corporations, and their subsidiaries"),
("RA6713-3C-GIFT-NOMINAL-EXCLUDED", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 3(c)", "medium",
 "A clerk at a city permit office receives an unsolicited box of native delicacies of insignificant value from a resident, with no favor expected now or later. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 3(c), how is this treated?",
 "It falls outside the Act's definition of a \"gift\"",
 [("It is a prohibited gift, since every gift to an employee is unlawful", R, "Sec. 3(c) expressly excludes an unsolicited gift of nominal or insignificant value given without any favor in view."),
  ("It must first be declared in the clerk's SALN before it is kept", S, "The SALN (Sec. 8) lists assets and liabilities; it is not a clearance for small unsolicited tokens."),
  ("It may be kept only with the written consent of the office head", R, "No consent rule applies; the head-of-office permission in Sec. 7(d) is only for foreign travel grants.")],
 "Gift (Sec. 3(c)): a thing or right disposed of gratuitously, including a simulated sale, but not an unsolicited gift of nominal value given without a favor in view.",
 "Unsolicited + insignificant value + no favor expected = not a \"gift\" under the Act.",
 "It shall not include an unsolicited gift of nominal or insignificant value not given in anticipation of, or in exchange for, a favor"),
("RA6713-3C-SIMULATED-SALE", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 3(c)", "medium",
 "A contractor \"sells\" a new car worth ₱1.2 million for ₱10,000 to the city engineer who inspects the contractor's projects. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 3(c), what is this transaction?",
 "A gift, because a simulated sale falls under the term",
 [("A valid sale, because the engineer paid an agreed price in cash", R, "Paying a token price does not cure it; Sec. 3(c) treats a simulated or ostensibly onerous sale as a gift."),
  ("A loan, because the car could later be returned", S, "A loan (Sec. 3(e)) is a separate term; nothing here is lent."),
  ("A divestment of the contractor's business interest", S, "Divestment (Sec. 3(j)) is an official giving up his own conflicting interest, not receiving property.")],
 "A \"simulated sale\" looks like a purchase but the price is not real; Sec. 3(c) counts it as a gift.",
 "A ₱1.2 million car for ₱10,000 is a gift dressed as a sale.",
 "shall include a simulated sale or an ostensibly onerous disposition thereof"),
("RA6713-3D-CHRISTMAS-NOT-EXEMPT", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 3(d)", "medium",
 "At Christmas, a supplier with a pending bid gives the procurement officer an expensive wine set. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 3(d), does the holiday occasion change anything?",
 "No; it is still \"receiving any gift\" since the value is not nominal",
 [("Yes; gifts given during national festivities are always exempt", R, "Sec. 3(d) says the act counts \"even on the occasion of\" a national festivity like Christmas."),
  ("Yes; it becomes allowed once the officer reports it to the Ombudsman", W, "No reporting rule turns such a gift into an allowed one; the Ombudsman's Sec. 7(d) regulations cover foreign-government gifts."),
  ("No, but only because the supplier is a juridical person", S, "Whether the giver is a natural or juridical person does not matter; the test is value and the favor in view.")],
 "\"Receiving any gift\" (Sec. 3(d)): accepting, directly or indirectly, a gift from a non-relative, even at a family celebration or national festivity, if its value is not nominal or a favor is expected.",
 "Christmas is not a loophole: check the value and the favor, not the date.",
 "even on the occasion of a family celebration or national festivity like Christmas, if the value of the gift is neither nominal nor insignificant"),
("RA6713-3E-LOAN-SCOPE", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 3(e)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 3(e), what does the term \"loan\" cover?",
 "Simple loan, commodatum, and guarantees or financing arrangements",
 [("Only cash loans that come from banks and lending companies", R, "Sec. 3(e) is not limited to cash or to banks; it also covers commodatum and guarantees."),
  ("Only loans charging interest above the legal rate of interest", R, "The Act does not define a loan by its interest rate."),
  ("Simple loan only; commodatum is outside the term", S, "Sec. 3(e) names both simple loan and commodatum.")],
 "Commodatum: a loan of a thing to be used and returned (for example, a borrowed car), as opposed to a simple loan of money or consumables.",
 "Loan here is broad: money, things lent for use, and guarantees.",
 "covers both simple loan and commodatum as well as guarantees, financing arrangements or accommodations intended to ensure its approval"),
("RA6713-3F-SUBSTANTIAL-STOCKHOLDER", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 3(f)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 3(f), who is a \"substantial stockholder\" of a corporation?",
 "One who owns enough shares to elect a director",
 [("One who owns at least 10% of the outstanding shares", R, "R.A. 6713 sets no percentage; the test is enough shares to elect a director."),
  ("One who owns a majority of the corporation's voting shares", R, "A majority is not required; enough shares to elect one director is enough."),
  ("One who sits on the corporation's board as its chairman", S, "Board membership is a separate ground of conflict of interest in Sec. 3(i), not the stockholder test.")],
 "Substantial stockholder (Sec. 3(f)): any person who owns, directly or indirectly, shares sufficient to elect a director; it also applies to parties to a voting trust.",
 "Can your shares elect one director? Then you are a substantial stockholder.",
 "shares of stock sufficient to elect a director of a corporation"),
("RA6713-3K-RELATIVES-DEGREE", "GI-DEADLINE-NUMBER", "Sec. 3(k)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 3(k), \"relatives\" covers persons related to the official up to what degree?",
 "Fourth civil degree of consanguinity or affinity",
 [("Third civil degree of consanguinity or affinity", N, "The Act sets the fourth degree, not the third."),
  ("Second civil degree of consanguinity only", N, "Too narrow: the fourth degree, and affinity counts too."),
  ("Fourth civil degree of consanguinity only", S, "Relatives by affinity (in-laws) are included, as are bilas, inso and balae.")],
 "Consanguinity is relation by blood; affinity is relation by marriage. Sec. 3(k) also names bilas, inso and balae.",
 "Four degrees, blood or marriage.",
 "within the fourth civil degree of consanguinity or affinity, including bilas, inso and balae"),
("RA6713-4B-MERIT-INCREASES", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 4(B)", "hard",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 4(B), what may the Civil Service Commission authorize for a limited number of employees whom office colleagues recognize as outstanding in observing ethical standards?",
 "Merit increases beyond regular progression steps",
 [("Automatic appointment to a permanent position", R, "Sec. 4(B) speaks of merit increases, not appointments."),
  ("Exemption from filing the annual SALN", R, "No one is exempted from the SALN for good conduct; Sec. 8(A) exempts only honorary, laborer, casual and temporary personnel."),
  ("A cash prize equal to six months' salary", N, "Six months' salary appears in Sec. 11 as the maximum fine, not as a reward.")],
 "Sec. 4(B) tells the CSC to promote the norms of conduct through information programs, workshops, merit increases and research on positive motivation.",
 "4(B) = CSC rewards ethics with pay steps beyond the normal ladder.",
 "workshops authorizing merit increases beyond regular progression steps, to a limited number of employees recognized by their office colleagues to be outstanding"),
("RA6713-5C-NEXT-IN-RANK-SIGNS", "GI-WHO-HOLDS-POWER", "Sec. 5(c)", "easy",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 5(c), who signs an official document when the duly authorized signatories are absent?",
 "The official next-in-rank or the officer in charge",
 [("The head of the agency's legal department", W, "Sec. 5(c) names the next-in-rank official or the officer in charge, not the legal office."),
  ("Any employee chosen by the person making the request", R, "The public cannot pick a signatory; the Act names who signs."),
  ("No one; the document waits for the signatories to return", R, "Waiting is what Sec. 5(c) prevents: documents must be processed within a reasonable time.")],
 "Sec. 5(c): process documents within a reasonable time, with no more than three signatories where practicable.",
 "Absent signatory? Next-in-rank or OIC signs, so the paper keeps moving.",
 "In the absence of duly authorized signatories, the official next-in-rank or officer in charge shall sign for and in their behalf."),
("RA6713-6-COA-CHAIR-MEMBER", "GI-WHO-HOLDS-POWER", "Sec. 6", "medium",
 "Apart from its two co-chairmen, which official sits on the R.A. 6713 Committee on Awards as a member, under Sec. 6?",
 "The Chairman of the Commission on Audit",
 [("The Secretary of Budget and Management", W, "The DBM Secretary is not named in Sec. 6."),
  ("The Chairman of the Commission on Elections", W, "COMELEC is a constitutional commission, but Sec. 6 names the COA Chairman."),
  ("The Executive Secretary of the President", W, "The President appoints two government employees as members; the Executive Secretary is not named.")],
 "Committee on Awards (Sec. 6): Ombudsman and CSC Chairman as co-chairmen; COA Chairman and two government employees appointed by the President as members.",
 "Ombudsman + CSC lead; COA joins with two presidential appointees.",
 "the Chairman of the Commission on Audit, and two government employees to be appointed by the President, as members"),
("RA6713-6-AWARD-CRITERIA", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 6", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 6, which of these must the Committee on Awards take into account when it confers awards?",
 "The obscurity of the position",
 [("The nominee's political party affiliation", R, "Considering party would contradict political neutrality; Sec. 6 does not list it."),
  ("The number of the nominee's subordinates", R, "Sec. 6 lists the level of salary and the obscurity of the position, not the size of one's staff."),
  ("The nominee's highest academic degree", R, "Educational attainment is not among the Sec. 6 factors.")],
 "Sec. 6 factors include years of service, quality and consistency of performance, obscurity of the position, level of salary, unique achievement, and the risks or temptations of the work.",
 "Sec. 6 favors the unseen, low-paid, tempted worker.",
 "the obscurity of the position, the level of salary, the unique and exemplary quality of a certain achievement, and the risks or temptations inherent in the work"),
("RA6713-6-AUTO-PROMOTION", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 6", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 6, what happens to the position of a public servant honored as an outstanding official or employee of the year?",
 "Automatic promotion to the next higher position",
 [("Permanent exemption from performance ratings", R, "Sec. 6 gives no exemption from ratings; it gives promotion."),
  ("A two-step salary increase in the same position", R, "Sec. 6 promotes the awardee to the next higher position with commensurate salary, not a step increase in place."),
  ("Security of tenure in the present post until retirement", R, "Tenure is not the Sec. 6 reward; the awardee moves up.")],
 "Sec. 6 rewards may include bonuses, citations, GOCC directorships, scholarships and paid vacations; awardees are also automatically promoted.",
 "Awardee of the year moves one rung up, automatically.",
 "They shall likewise be automatically promoted to the next higher position with the commensurate salary suitable to their qualifications."),
("RA6713-6-REWARD-FORMS", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 6", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 6, which is listed as a possible incentive for outstanding public officials and employees?",
 "Directorships in government-owned or controlled corporations",
 [("Exemption from income tax for one year", R, "Tax exemption is not among the Sec. 6 incentives."),
  ("Eligibility for any government post without examination", R, "Sec. 6 does not grant civil service eligibility."),
  ("Immunity from administrative complaints for the year", R, "No award protects an official from complaints.")],
 "Sec. 6 incentives: bonuses, citations, directorships in GOCCs, local and foreign scholarship grants, paid vacations and the like.",
 "Think recognition and opportunity, never exemption or immunity.",
 "may take the form of bonuses, citations, directorships in government-owned or controlled corporations, local and foreign scholarship grants, paid vacations and the like"),
("RA6713-7B-FORMER-OFFICE-PRACTICE", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 7(b)", "hard",
 "A lawyer resigns from the Bureau of Customs. Six months later, a private client asks the lawyer to handle a case pending before the Bureau. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 7(b), may the lawyer take it?",
 "No; for one year the lawyer cannot practice on matters before the former office",
 [("Yes; restrictions on private practice end the day the lawyer resigns", R, "Sec. 7(b) keeps a one-year bar on practice in matters before the former office."),
  ("Yes, provided the lawyer first gets a clearance from the CSC", W, "No CSC clearance lifts the bar; the Act fixes the one-year period."),
  ("No; former officials are barred from every kind of private practice for five years", N, "Five years is the Sec. 11 prison term; the practice bar is one year and only for matters before the former office.")],
 "Sec. 7(b)(2) allows private practice after separation, except that for one year the professional cannot practice in any matter before the office he used to be with.",
 "Left the office? Wait one year before appearing against it.",
 "the professional concerned cannot practice his profession in connection with any matter before the office he used to be with, in which case the one-year prohibition shall likewise apply"),
("RA6713-7D-FOREIGN-FELLOWSHIP", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 7(d)", "medium",
 "A foreign government offers a public hospital nurse a fully funded fellowship abroad. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 7(d), how is the offer treated?",
 "It may be accepted, because Congress consents to fellowship grants",
 [("It must be refused, because no gift from a foreign government may be accepted", R, "Sec. 7(d) lists foreign gifts Congress consents to, including scholarships and fellowships."),
  ("It may be accepted only if its value is merely nominal", S, "The nominal-value test is for souvenirs, item (i); fellowships are a separate item (ii)."),
  ("It may be accepted only after the Senate ratifies it", W, "No Senate ratification is needed; Congress already gave consent in the Act.")],
 "Sec. 7(d) foreign-government gifts Congress consents to: (i) nominal souvenirs; (ii) scholarship or fellowship grants or medical treatment; (iii) travel grants abroad, if permitted by the head of office.",
 "Learning and healing from abroad are allowed: scholarships, fellowships, medical treatment.",
 "The acceptance by a public official or employee of a gift in the nature of a scholarship or fellowship grant or medical treatment"),
("RA6713-7D-TRAVEL-GRANT-HEAD-PERMIT", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 7(d)", "hard",
 "A foreign government offers to pay a city engineer's travel to a course held entirely outside the Philippines. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 7(d), besides being consistent with Philippine interests, what must the acceptance have?",
 "Permission from the head of the engineer's office",
 [("Prior approval from the Department of Foreign Affairs", W, "Sec. 7(d)(iii) requires the permission of the head of office, branch or agency, not the DFA."),
  ("A value no greater than the engineer's monthly salary", R, "Travel grants may be of more than nominal value; no salary cap is set."),
  ("A written waiver from the Office of the Ombudsman", W, "The Ombudsman writes regulations for this subsection but does not issue case-by-case waivers under the text.")],
 "Sec. 7(d)(iii): travel grants or expenses for travel entirely outside the Philippines, of more than nominal value, if appropriate or consistent with Philippine interests and permitted by the head of office.",
 "Foreign-paid trip abroad: the boss must say yes.",
 "permitted by the head of office, branch or agency to which he belongs"),
("RA6713-7D-OMBUDSMAN-REGULATIONS", "GI-WHO-HOLDS-POWER", "Sec. 7(d)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 7(d), which office prescribes the regulations, including reporting and disclosure rules, for gifts and grants from foreign governments?",
 "The Ombudsman",
 [("The Civil Service Commission", W, "The CSC administers the Act generally (Sec. 12), but Sec. 7(d) gives this rule-making to the Ombudsman."),
  ("The Department of Foreign Affairs", W, "The DFA is not mentioned in Sec. 7(d)."),
  ("The Commission on Audit", W, "COA audits public funds; Sec. 7(d) does not give it this role.")],
 "Sec. 7(d) ends: \"The Ombudsman shall prescribe such regulations as may be necessary to carry out the purpose of this subsection.\"",
 "Foreign gifts: the Ombudsman writes the reporting rules.",
 "The Ombudsman shall prescribe such regulations as may be necessary to carry out the purpose of this subsection, including pertinent reporting and disclosure requirements."),
("RA6713-8A-SALN-EXEMPT", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 8(A)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(A), which group is NOT required to file a Statement of Assets, Liabilities and Net Worth?",
 "Laborers and casual or temporary workers",
 [("Military and police personnel in active service", R, "Military and police personnel are public officials under Sec. 3(b) and are not exempted."),
  ("Elected barangay officials serving their first term", R, "Elective local officials file their statements; no first-term exemption exists."),
  ("Employees who received no salary increase that year", R, "Salary changes do not affect the duty to file.")],
 "Sec. 8(A) exempts only those who serve in an honorary capacity, laborers, and casual or temporary workers.",
 "Exempt from the SALN: honorary, laborers, casual or temporary. Everyone else files.",
 "except those who serve in an honorary capacity, laborers and casual or temporary workers"),
("RA6713-8A-SPOUSES-JOINT-OR-SEPARATE", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 8(A)", "easy",
 "A husband and wife both work in government. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(A), how may they file their required statements?",
 "Jointly or separately, as they choose",
 [("Separately only, one statement for each spouse", S, "Sec. 8(A) allows either joint or separate filing."),
  ("Jointly only, under the higher-ranking spouse", R, "No rank rule exists; joint filing is an option, not a requirement."),
  ("Only the spouse who earns more files a statement", R, "Both spouses are covered; they may simply file together or apart.")],
 "Sec. 8(A): \"Husband and wife who are both public officials or employees may file the required statements jointly or separately.\"",
 "Both in government? Their choice: one joint SALN or two.",
 "Husband and wife who are both public officials or employees may file the required statements jointly or separately."),
("RA6713-8A-JUDGE-FILES-COURT-ADMIN", "GI-WHO-HOLDS-POWER", "Sec. 8(A)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(A), with whom does a Regional Trial Court judge file the SALN?",
 "The Court Administrator",
 [("The Clerk of Court of the Supreme Court", W, "Justices file with the Clerk of Court of the Supreme Court; judges file with the Court Administrator."),
  ("The Judicial and Bar Council", W, "The JBC screens nominees; it does not receive SALNs under Sec. 8(A)."),
  ("The Civil Service Commission", W, "The CSC receives statements of \"all other\" officials; judges have their own office.")],
 "Sec. 8(A) filing offices include: Justices with the Clerk of Court of the Supreme Court; Judges with the Court Administrator.",
 "Justices to the SC Clerk of Court; judges to the Court Administrator.",
 "Justices, with the Clerk of Court of the Supreme Court; Judges, with the Court Administrator"),
("RA6713-8A-LOCAL-FILES-DEPUTY-OMB", "GI-WHO-HOLDS-POWER", "Sec. 8(A)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(A), with which office does a municipal councilor in Leyte file the SALN?",
 "The Deputy Ombudsman for that region",
 [("The regional office of the Civil Service Commission", W, "Regional and local officials file with the Deputy Ombudsman in their region."),
  ("The Office of the President", W, "The Office of the President receives statements of national executive officials and senior military officers."),
  ("The office of the provincial governor", W, "A governor is not a filing office under Sec. 8(A).")],
 "Sec. 8(A)(3): regional and local officials and employees file with the Deputy Ombudsman in their respective regions.",
 "Local official? File with the Deputy Ombudsman of the region.",
 "Regional and local officials and employees, with the Deputy Ombudsman in their respective regions"),
("RA6713-8A-AFP-COLONEL-FILES-OP", "GI-WHO-HOLDS-POWER", "Sec. 8(A)", "hard",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(A), where does an Armed Forces officer holding the rank of colonel file the SALN?",
 "The Office of the President",
 [("The Deputy Ombudsman in the officer's region", W, "That office receives statements of officers below the rank of colonel or naval captain."),
  ("The Department of National Defense", W, "The DND is not a filing office under Sec. 8(A)."),
  ("The Civil Service Commission", W, "The CSC receives the statements of officials not covered by the other categories.")],
 "Sec. 8(A)(4): officers from the rank of colonel or naval captain file with the Office of the President; lower ranks file with the Deputy Ombudsman in their region.",
 "Colonel and up: Office of the President. Below: Deputy Ombudsman.",
 "Officers of the armed forces from the rank of colonel or naval captain, with the Office of the President"),
("RA6713-8A-OTHERS-FILE-CSC", "GI-WHO-HOLDS-POWER", "Sec. 8(A)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(A), which office receives the SALN of public officials and employees not covered by any of the other listed categories?",
 "The Civil Service Commission",
 [("The national office of the Ombudsman", W, "The national Ombudsman office receives statements of constitutional and national elective officials."),
  ("The Commission on Audit", W, "COA is not a filing office under Sec. 8(A)."),
  ("The Office of the President", W, "The Office of the President receives statements of national executive officials and senior military officers.")],
 "Sec. 8(A)(5): all other public officials and employees, as defined in R.A. 3019, file with the Civil Service Commission.",
 "Not a justice, judge, local, national elective, executive or senior AFP officer? File with the CSC.",
 "All other public officials and employees, defined in Republic Act No. 3019, as amended, with the Civil Service Commission"),
("RA6713-8C-COPY-FEE", "GI-TERM-MATCH", "Sec. 8(C)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(C), what must a person pay to get a copy of an official's filed statement?",
 "A reasonable fee for reproduction, mailing and certification",
 [("Nothing, since filed statements are public documents", R, "The statements are open to the public, but Sec. 8(C)(3) still requires a reasonable fee."),
  ("A fixed fee of ₱25,000 for each statement requested", N, "₱25,000 is the Sec. 11 cap on the penalty for misusing a statement, not a copy fee."),
  ("A documentary stamp tax set by the Bureau of Internal Revenue", W, "The fee covers costs and is not a BIR tax.")],
 "Sec. 8(C): statements are open for inspection at reasonable hours, may be copied after 10 working days, and copies cost a reasonable fee.",
 "Copies are public but not free: you pay the cost.",
 "Any person requesting a copy of a statement shall be required to pay a reasonable fee to cover the cost of reproduction and mailing of such statement, as well as the cost of certification."),
("RA6713-8C-TEN-YEARS-AVAILABLE", "GI-DEADLINE-NUMBER", "Sec. 8(C)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(C), for how long after receipt must a filed statement stay available to the public?",
 "10 years",
 [("10 working days", N, "Ten working days is when a statement may first be copied, not how long it stays available."),
  ("5 years", N, "Five years is the Sec. 11 maximum prison term."),
  ("1 year", N, "One year is the post-separation period in Sec. 7(b).")],
 "Sec. 8(C)(4): statements are available for ten years after receipt; afterward they may be destroyed unless needed in an ongoing investigation.",
 "Ten working days to copy, ten years to keep.",
 "Any statement filed under this Act shall be available to the public for a period of ten (10) years after receipt of the statement."),
("RA6713-8D-COMMERCIAL-USE-BARRED", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 8(D)", "medium",
 "A lending company collects officials' filed statements to market loans to wealthy officials. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 8(D), is this allowed?",
 "No; commercial use is barred, except news reporting by the media",
 [("Yes; filed statements are public documents, so any use at all is allowed", R, "Public access is for accountability; Sec. 8(D) bars commercial use and uses contrary to morals or public policy."),
  ("Yes, as long as the company pays the reproduction fee", S, "Paying the Sec. 8(C) fee gives access, not permission for a prohibited use."),
  ("No; only the Ombudsman may ever look at a filed statement", R, "Too strong: anyone may inspect the statements at reasonable hours under Sec. 8(C).")],
 "Sec. 8(D): no one may obtain or use a statement for any purpose contrary to morals or public policy, or for any commercial purpose other than by news and communications media for dissemination to the general public.",
 "Read it for accountability or news; never to sell something.",
 "any commercial purpose other than by news and communications media for dissemination to the general public"),
("RA6713-11D-MISUSE-PENALTY-25K", "GI-DEADLINE-NUMBER", "Sec. 11(d)", "hard",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 11(d), an official may sue a person who misuses the official's filed statement. Up to how much penalty may the court assess?",
 "₱25,000",
 [("₱5,000", N, "₱5,000 is the maximum fine for violating Sections 7, 8 or 9."),
  ("₱50,000", N, "The Act sets ₱25,000 as the ceiling."),
  ("₱10,000", N, "The Act sets ₱25,000 as the ceiling.")],
 "Sec. 11(d): the court may assess a penalty in any amount not exceeding ₱25,000 against a person who obtains or uses a report for a purpose prohibited by Sec. 8(D).",
 "Misusing a SALN: up to ₱25,000.",
 "may assess against such person a penalty in any amount not to exceed twenty-five thousand pesos (P25,000)"),
("RA6713-9-PARTNERSHIP-COVERED", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 9", "medium",
 "An official is a partner in a firm whose interests conflict with the official's duties. Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 9, do the resignation and divestment rules apply?",
 "Yes; the same rule applies to a partner in a partnership",
 [("No; the rules cover only stockholders of corporations", S, "Sec. 9 expressly extends the rule to partners in a partnership."),
  ("No, as long as the partnership is registered with the SEC", R, "Registration does not remove the conflict; Sec. 9 makes no such exception."),
  ("Yes, but only when the official holds a majority interest", R, "Sec. 9 has no majority-interest condition for partners.")],
 "Sec. 9: resign from the private enterprise within 30 days and divest within 60 days; the same rule applies to a partner in a partnership.",
 "Corporation or partnership, the divestment rule is the same.",
 "The same rule shall apply where the public official or employee is a partner in a partnership."),
("RA6713-10B-GOOD-FAITH-OPINION", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 10(b)", "hard",
 "A member of the House acts in good faith on a written opinion interpreting R.A. 6713 that the designated House committee issued and the House approved. Under Sec. 10(b), what follows?",
 "The member is not subject to any sanction under the Act",
 [("The member is still liable, but with a lighter penalty", R, "Sec. 10(b) removes the sanction altogether for good-faith reliance."),
  ("Only the committee that issued the opinion is protected", R, "The protection is for the person who relies on the opinion and others in a similar situation."),
  ("The member must still get the CSC's approval of the act", W, "Sec. 10(b) gives this opinion power to the committees of Congress, not the CSC.")],
 "Sec. 10(b): designated committees of both Houses may render written opinions interpreting the Act, subject to approval by majority vote of the House concerned.",
 "Followed an approved official opinion in good faith? No sanction.",
 "who, after issuance of the opinion acts in good faith in accordance with it shall not be subject to any sanction provided in this Act"),
("RA6713-11A-SUSPENSION-ONE-YEAR", "GI-DEADLINE-NUMBER", "Sec. 11(a)", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 11(a), what is the longest suspension that may be imposed on an official who violates the Act?",
 "One year",
 [("Six months", N, "Six months' salary is the maximum fine; the suspension can run up to one year."),
  ("Five years", N, "Five years is the maximum prison term for violating Sections 7, 8 or 9."),
  ("Ninety days", R, "The Act does not set a 90-day cap.")],
 "Sec. 11(a): fine of up to six months' salary, suspension of up to one year, or removal, depending on the gravity of the offense.",
 "Fine: 6 months' pay. Suspension: 1 year. Prison: 5 years.",
 "suspension not exceeding one (1) year"),
("RA6713-11B-ADMIN-PROOF-ENOUGH", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 11(b)", "medium",
 "An employee's violation of R.A. 6713 is proven in an administrative case, and no criminal case is ever filed. Under Sec. 11(b), may the employee be dismissed?",
 "Yes; proof in the administrative case is sufficient cause",
 [("No; a criminal conviction must come first", R, "Sec. 11(b) says removal may follow even if no criminal prosecution is instituted."),
  ("No; without a criminal conviction, only a fine may be imposed", R, "Removal is available on administrative proof alone."),
  ("Yes, but only with the President's written approval", W, "The Act requires no presidential approval for dismissal.")],
 "Administrative and criminal liability are separate; Sec. 11(b) lets an administrative finding alone justify removal.",
 "Admin case proven = enough to dismiss, criminal case or not.",
 "Any violation hereof proven in a proper administrative proceeding shall be sufficient cause for removal or dismissal of a public official or employee, even if no criminal prosecution is instituted against him."),
("RA6713-11C-PRIVATE-CONSPIRATORS", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 11(c)", "medium",
 "A private supplier conspires with a procurement officer to violate R.A. 6713. Under Sec. 11(c), what liability does the supplier face?",
 "The same penal liabilities as the officer, tried jointly",
 [("None, since the Act covers only public officials", R, "Sec. 11(c) expressly reaches private individuals who conspire with public officials."),
  ("Only civil damages, payable to the government", R, "The liability is penal, the same as the official's."),
  ("A fine only, because the supplier holds no office", R, "The supplier faces the same penal liabilities, not a fine-only rule.")],
 "Sec. 11(c): private individuals who participate as co-principals, accomplices or accessories share the officials' penal liabilities and are tried jointly with them.",
 "Conspire with an official, share the official's penalty.",
 "shall be subject to the same penal liabilities as the public officials or employees and shall be tried jointly with them"),
("RA6713-12-OMBUDSMAN-PROTECTS-WHISTLEBLOWERS", "GI-WHO-HOLDS-POWER", "Sec. 12", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 12, which office must take steps to protect citizens who denounce acts of public officials that violate the Act?",
 "The Ombudsman",
 [("The Civil Service Commission", W, "The CSC administers and enforces the Act, but Sec. 12 assigns protection of complainants to the Ombudsman."),
  ("The Department of Justice", W, "The DOJ is not named in Sec. 12."),
  ("The Commission on Human Rights", W, "The CHR is not named in R.A. 6713.")],
 "Sec. 12: the CSC has primary responsibility for administering the Act; the Ombudsman protects citizens who denounce violations.",
 "CSC runs the Act; the Ombudsman shields those who report.",
 "The Ombudsman shall likewise take steps to protect citizens who denounce acts or omissions of public officials and employees which are in violation of this Act."),
("RA6713-13-STRICTER-STANDARDS", "GI-SCENARIO-APPLY", "Sec. 13", "medium",
 "An agency's own code bans its employees from accepting any gift at all, which is stricter than R.A. 6713. Under Sec. 13, is the agency rule affected?",
 "No; the Act does not derogate from more stringent standards",
 [("Yes; R.A. 6713 is the only standard agencies may apply", R, "Sec. 13 keeps stricter laws and agency rules in force."),
  ("Yes, unless Congress first approves the agency rule", W, "No congressional approval is required by Sec. 13."),
  ("No, but it binds only employees hired after 1989", R, "Sec. 13 has no hiring-date condition.")],
 "Sec. 13: nothing in the Act derogates from any law or regulation that sets more stringent standards for an agency's officials and employees.",
 "R.A. 6713 is a floor, not a ceiling.",
 "Nothing in this Act shall be construed to derogate from any law, or any regulation prescribed by any body or agency, which provides for more stringent standards for its official and employees."),
("RA6713-17-EFFECTIVITY", "GI-DEADLINE-NUMBER", "Sec. 17", "medium",
 "Under R.A. 6713, Sec. 17, when does the Act take effect?",
 "30 days after publication is completed in the Official Gazette or two newspapers",
 [("15 days after its publication in the Official Gazette", N, "Fifteen days is the general Civil Code rule; Sec. 17 sets 30 days."),
  ("Immediately upon its approval by the President on February 20, 1989", R, "February 20, 1989 is the approval date, not the effectivity date."),
  ("60 days after its publication in any newspaper of general circulation", N, "Sixty days is the Sec. 9 divestment period; Sec. 17 sets 30 days.")],
 "Sec. 17: the Act takes effect after 30 days following completion of its publication in the Official Gazette or in two national newspapers of general circulation.",
 "Approved Feb. 20, 1989; effective 30 days after publication.",
 "This Act shall take effect after thirty (30) days following the completion of its publication in the Official Gazette or in two (2) national newspapers of general circulation."),
]
